---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Speaking"
  description="Adrian Lee speaks on community strategy, platform safety, and AI governance. Available for conferences, executive offsites, and policy convenings."
>
  <div class="speaking-page" style="padding-top: var(--nav-h);">
    <div class="page-header">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="label">Speaking</span></div>
        <h1 class="page-header__title">
          Talks grounded in<br>
          <em>frontline operations.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="page-header__desc">
          Keynotes and workshops on community strategy, platform safety, and practical AI governance. 
          Focused on real case studies, operational systems, and actionable takeaways for your audience.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: var(--space-6); display: inline-flex;" id="speaking-book-hero">
          Book Adrian for your event →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- KEYNOTE TOPICS -->
    <section class="topics section" aria-labelledby="topics-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="label">Keynote topics</span></div>
        <h2 id="topics-heading">Signature talks</h2>

        <div class="topics__grid">

          <div class="topic__card card" id="talk-1">
            <div class="topic__number">Talk 01</div>
            <h3>The Governance Gap: Why Communities Collapse and AI Deployments Stall</h3>
            <div class="topic__badges">
              <span class="badge badge--community">Community</span>
              <span class="badge badge--ai">AI Governance</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              The structural failures that repeatedly degrade online communities are 
              now showing up in autonomous AI agent rollouts. This talk examines the shared failure modes, 
              explains how to identify governance gaps early, and offers practical controls to keep systems stable.
            </p>
            <div class="topic__details">
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Format</span>
                <span>45 to 60 minute keynote, or 90 minute interactive workshop</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Best for</span>
                <span>Technology conferences, policy forums, executive leadership teams</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Key takeaways</span>
                <ul>
                  <li>The 5 operational governance failures common to social platforms and AI agents</li>
                  <li>Diagnostic checkpoints to evaluate platform risk before expanding access</li>
                  <li>Participatory principles that keep automation accountable</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="topic__card card" id="talk-2">
            <div class="topic__number">Talk 02</div>
            <h3>Building Communities That Last: From First Member to Global Ecosystem</h3>
            <div class="topic__badges">
              <span class="badge badge--community">Community</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              A candid walk through a decade of community building across gaming, 
              Web3, and tech platforms. What early cohorts teach you that playbooks miss, 
              and the architectural choices that determine whether a platform survives past year two.
            </p>
            <div class="topic__details">
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Format</span>
                <span>30 to 60 minute keynote</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Best for</span>
                <span>Community conferences, startup summits, product strategy offsites</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Key takeaways</span>
                <ul>
                  <li>The 0-to-1 community architecture framework</li>
                  <li>Why community initiatives often stall after initial hype</li>
                  <li>Metrics that separate active participation from vanity numbers</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="topic__card card" id="talk-3">
            <div class="topic__number">Talk 03</div>
            <h3>Moderation at Human Scale: Platform Safety Without Burning People Out</h3>
            <div class="topic__badges">
              <span class="badge badge--ai">Platform Safety</span>
              <span class="badge badge--community">Community</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Moderation is fundamentally an organizational and human challenge, not just an algorithmic filter. 
              This talk presents system architectures that protect community standards while shielding 
              the teams on the frontlines from psychological burnout.
            </p>
            <div class="topic__details">
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Format</span>
                <span>45 minute keynote or half-day masterclass</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Best for</span>
                <span>Trust and safety teams, operations leads, platform policymakers</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Key takeaways</span>
                <ul>
                  <li>Tiered moderation models that scale sustainably</li>
                  <li>Protocols to prevent operational moderator exhaustion</li>
                  <li>Auditing tools to measure the health of moderation workflows</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SPEAKING LOGISTICS -->
    <section class="logistics section--sm" aria-labelledby="logistics-heading">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="label">Event details</span></div>
        <h2 id="logistics-heading">Logistics &amp; planning</h2>

        <div class="logistics__grid">
          <div class="logistics__item">
            <span class="logistics__icon">📍</span>
            <h3>Location</h3>
            <p>Based in Singapore. Available throughout Asia Pacific and globally for keynotes and tailored workshops.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="logistics__item">
            <span class="logistics__icon">🎯</span>
            <h3>Customization</h3>
            <p>Every presentation is adapted to the specific audience, industry, and goals of your event.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="logistics__item">
            <span class="logistics__icon">📅</span>
            <h3>Lead time</h3>
            <p>Please reach out 4 to 6 weeks in advance for keynote sessions, and 8+ weeks for full-day workshops.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="logistics__item">
            <span class="logistics__icon">💬</span>
            <h3>Initial details needed</h3>
            <p>Event date, location, expected audience profile, and the primary takeaway you want attendees to leave with.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SPEAKING CTA -->
    <section class="speaking-cta section--sm" aria-labelledby="speaking-cta-heading">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="card card--featured speaking-cta__card">
          <h2 id="speaking-cta-heading">Book Adrian for your event</h2>
          <p>Send your event outline and I will reply within 48 hours regarding availability and scope.</p>
          <a href="/contact?type=speaking" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" id="speaking-book-cta">Send speaking inquiry →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
/* TOPICS */
.topics h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-10); }
.topics__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); }
.topic__card { padding: var(--space-8); }
.topic__number { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--terracotta); letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.topic__card h3 { font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.topic__badges { display: flex; gap: var(--space-2); flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: var(--space-5); }
.topic__card > p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
.topic__details { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-4); background: var(--bg-elevated); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: var(--space-6); }
.topic__detail { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 100px 1fr; gap: var(--space-4); }
.topic__detail .label { font-size: 0.7rem; padding-top: 2px; }
.topic__detail span:last-child { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
.topic__detail ul { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); }
.topic__detail li::before { content: '→ '; color: var(--terracotta); }
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .topic__detail { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-2); }
}

/* LOGISTICS */
.logistics h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-10); }
.logistics__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: var(--space-5); }
.logistics__item { padding: var(--space-6); background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); }
.logistics__icon { font-size: 1.5rem; display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.logistics__item h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
.logistics__item p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.65; }
@media (max-width: 600px) { .logistics__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

/* CTA */
.speaking-cta__card { padding: var(--space-10); text-align: center; }
.speaking-cta__card h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.speaking-cta__card > p { color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); max-width: 440px; margin-inline: auto; margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
</style>
